--[[
	waves_test.luau — unit + oracle tests for `src/shared/sim/Waves.luau` and
	`src/shared/sim/Shop.luau` (`SIM-SPEC.md` §S1: transcription, not redesign).

	HOW TO RUN
	----------
	    cd roblox/test && luau -O2 waves_test.luau

	No arguments needed: `Content.luau` self-loads its embedded `content.json`,
	and the oracle vectors are embedded below. Exits non-zero on any failure.

	THE ORACLE
	----------
	Every `ORACLE_*` value below was produced by RUNNING THE RUST (`CONTRACTS.md`
	C4's rule, applied to the sim layer) — never hand-derived, and never read back
	out of the Luau under test, which would make this file assert the port against
	itself and destroy the only thing that makes the port trustworthy.

	The generator is a throwaway crate with a path dependency on
	`sim-core/crates/sim` that touches only that crate's PUBLIC surface:

	  * `content::enemy_hp_mult(tick)` is `pub`, so the ramp curve is oracled
	    directly — raw `Fixed` values, plus the ×10000 post-step tiers.
	  * `waves::spawn` and `shop::generate_offers` are `pub(crate)`, so they are
	    driven through `sim::step` on a state rigged to isolate them:
	    `weapons.clear()` (no projectiles / hazards / minions, so `next_entity_id`
	    moves only for spawns), `enemies.clear()` before every tick (so `s.enemies`
	    after the step IS that tick's spawn list), and a tank pinned at 1e9 hp (so
	    the `dead` short-circuit never fires and nothing perturbs the streams).
	  * For the shop rows the generator sets `s.round = round + 1` and
	    `s.tick = round * ROUND_TICKS` before each step, so `step`'s round-boundary
	    branch regenerates the offers at a CHOSEN, FIXED round. That is what makes
	    the round-dependent rarity ramp (`shop.rs::rarity_weights`) observable at
	    all: the offers are drawn in two stages — a tier from a round-interpolated
	    weight table, then a uniform pick inside that tier.

	The per-tick / per-generation `rng_*` state is the load-bearing assertion:
	`Rng.below` is a rejection loop that consumes a VARIABLE number of u32 words,
	so a state match over a CONTIGUOUS run proves the draw ORDER, COUNT and
	CONDITIONS all match the Rust (`SIM-SPEC.md` §S4). One extra or skipped draw
	shows up immediately, and the run stops at the first divergent tick because
	everything after it is noise.

	WHAT IS DERIVED, NOT PINNED
	---------------------------
	Anything that lives in `content.json` — wave gates and cadences, enemy stats,
	roster size, the ramp's `(num, den)` parameters, both timelines — is read off
	`Content` at test time rather than copied into a literal here. The catalog is
	REGENERATED from the Rust tables on every balance pass, so a test carrying its
	own copy of catalog data goes stale silently. Only values that are a function
	of Rust *code* (the curve, the draw sequences) are pinned, and those come from
	the generator above.

	WHAT IS NOT TESTED HERE, AND WHY
	--------------------------------
	`Input::Reroll` and `Input::BuyOffer` live in `input.rs`, so by SIM-SPEC §S2
	they belong to `Input.luau`, not to `Shop.luau`. The reroll test below drives
	a LOCAL MIRROR of that branch structure (labelled as such) purely to prove
	the property `Shop.luau` owns: the offer stream advances exactly once per
	SUCCESSFUL reroll and not at all on the ignored branch.
]]

